// Motion Prompt #214 · MIT License (c) 2026 Shohei Ohtaki · https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/#214
//
// Embroidery / 刺繍
// Pack: artstyle (Art styles for image generation) · element 22 · Category: Digital, 3D & materials
// What happens: The same line drawing becomes embroidery in colored thread on fabric, with the stitches and the weave of the cloth visible.
// Motion spec:
//   - Material: fabric and colored thread
//   - Look: the direction of each stitch and the weave of the cloth are visible
//   - Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)
// When to use it: For merchandise, packaging or seasonal greetings that should feel warm and hand-made.
// Tags: embroidery, stitch, thread, fabric, textile, handmade
// Size: 539x208 px · Cycle: 4.7 s
// Needs: kit artstyle -> https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js
// Live demo: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/#214
//
// cells[i](k, w, h, u): k = CanvasRenderingContext2D (already cleared and wrapped in save/restore by the caller), w,h = size, u = seconds in [0, cycle). The picture depends only on u.
// Element code starts here. CELLS, constants and helpers live in the kit.

// @element 22
// 刺繍: 布に色糸を縫い込んで描く
CELLS[21] = (k, w, h, u) => gafu(k, w, h, u, '22');
